# Smoke Coverage Audit — Part 2: Coverage Rules & Domain Rollup (Crypto to AI)

File: openOODA/audit/smoke_coverage_audit_part2.oot
Logline: Defines 3-tier coverage classification rules and rolls up module counts across Core Infrastructure, Math, Network, and AI domains.

Setup: Classifies 12,478 std/ modules into COVERED, COVERED_BY_IMPORT_STUB, and UNCOVERED categories.

Beats:
  1. Three-tier coverage classification rules (COVERED, COVERED_BY_IMPORT_STUB, UNCOVERED).
  2. Fixture naming rules and conventions.
  3. Domain rollup: Crypto & security-critical (1,019 modules).
  4. Domain rollup: Math, algorithms, network, OS, concurrency, compilers, 3D, and AI.

================================================================
BEAT 2 — COVERAGE CLASSIFICATION RULES
================================================================

After the parallel stub cleanup finishes, every std/ module falls into
exactly one of three classes:

  COVERED
      A hand-written real smoke fixture exists at fixtures/*_smoke.oo
      whose import statement names the module. Asserts correctness
      (KAT, round-trip, expect_eq, expect_true, process_exit(1) on
      assertion failure, or `if got == want { OK } else { FAIL }`).
      20 modules qualify (see part 1).

  COVERED_BY_IMPORT_STUB
      A *_smoke.oo fixture exists and exercises the module's
      import, but the body has no functional assertion. These
      verify that the module at least compiles. 30 modules qualify
      (see part 1). Wave 2 should prefer upgrading one of these
      before writing a brand-new fixture.

  UNCOVERED
      No smoke fixture exists at all. Total: 12,478 - 20 - 30 =
      12,428 modules.

Naming convention for new smoke fixtures (used in the Wave 2
recommendations below):

      std/<sub>/<sub2>/<name>.oo  ->  fixtures/<sub>_<sub2>_<name>_smoke.oo

Exceptions used by the 20 real fixtures already in tree:
      std/net/http_req.oo     -> fixtures/http_req_smoke.oo
      std/net/http_resp.oo    -> fixtures/http_resp_smoke.oo
      std/net/ip_cidr.oo      -> fixtures/ip_cidr_smoke.oo
      std/encoding/hex_ct.oo  -> fixtures/hex_ct_smoke.oo
      std/crypto/chacha20_poly1305.oo -> fixtures/chacha20_poly1305_smoke.oo

Wave 2 should adopt the same drop-leading-std convention so the
existing fixture loader (which expects fixtures/<short>_smoke.oo)
keeps working without changes.

================================================================
BEAT 3 — DOMAIN ROLLUP (PART A: CORE & COMPUTING)
================================================================

Module counts grouped by domain. The 5,888 files in formal_proofs/
are auto-generated product-proof files (one verify_prove_prod_*
function per imported target module) and are not smoke fixtures;
they are catalogued separately in part 5. The 397 files in
proof_verifiers/ are a mix of in-tree deterministic verify_*
functions and adversarial fixtures that the existing smoke harness
already exercises. Both categories are excluded from the Wave 2
top-priority list because they are not first-class public APIs.

